--------------------------------------------------
	    How claude fix memory issue.
--------------------------------------------------
Root cause: UE4 4.26's Vulkan memory allocator had two bugs that only surface with NVIDIA driver 535+ on RTX 40xx GPUs.

Fix 1 — VulkanMemory.cpp (UE4): Stale AllocationSize after retry

When a 32MB page allocation failed, the code retried with the actual buffer size (e.g. 2MB) but then called Map(32MB) on the 2MB allocation → segfault. Added AllocationSize = Size after the retry.

Fix 2 — VulkanMemory.cpp (UE4): HOST_CACHED fallback

When the HOST_CACHED memory type (TypeIndex=3) failed entirely — as it does on this GPU/driver — the allocator had no fallback and crashed. Added a graceful fallback to HOST_COHERENT-only (TypeIndex=2).

Fix 3 — VulkanTexture.cpp (UE4): Wrong buffer usage flags

The CPUReadback staging buffer was created with BufferCreateInfo.usage = BufferMemFlags (memory property flags used as usage flags by mistake). Changed to the correct VK_BUFFER_USAGE_TRANSFER_DST_BIT.

Fix 4 — PixelReader.cpp (CARLA): Per-frame VkBuffer allocation

CARLA was creating and destroying a new FRHIGPUTextureReadback every single camera frame, causing repeated failed Vulkan allocation attempts and high overhead. Changed to a static cache per render target — the VkBuffer is now
